{"step_index":2178,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T09:49:34Z","input_tokens":2541,"cache_read_tokens":186566,"output_tokens":2349,"content":"# Phase 4 Implementation Report: Problem Search, Advanced Filters, Sorting, Pagination, Unique Routes & Duplicate Prevention\n\nPhase 4 has been completed. The **DSA Learning Hub** now includes functional multi-dimensional search, comprehensive status and topic filters (including **Review** status), 8-way sorting, responsive pagination with custom page sizes, direct URL hash routing (`#dsa/problem/:id`), and an import engine with duplicate prevention.\n\nAll existing code, animations, step execution, and visualizer features were preserved, and the execution engine remains untouched.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Summary of Implemented Features\n\n#### A. Search & Multi-Dimensional Filtering\n* **Full-Text Problem Search**:\n  * Real-time search across problem titles, LeetCode numbers, algorithmic patterns, problem descriptions, original summaries, and associated topics.\n  * Instant search clear button (`✕`) to reset query with one click.\n* **Topic Filter**:\n  * Dropdown covering all **30 curated DSA topics** (Arrays, Strings, Hash Maps, Two Pointers, Sliding Window, Prefix Sum, Binary Search, Sorting, Linked Lists, Stacks, Queues, Recursion, Backtracking, Trees, BSTs, Heaps, Graphs, BFS, DFS, Greedy, DP, Bit Manipulation, Tries, Union-Find, Topological Sort, Intervals, Monotonic Stack/Queue, Math, Matrix, Advanced Data Structures).\n  * Automatically filters problems via multi-topic tags (`topics: [...]`).\n* **Difficulty Filter**:\n  * One-click filter pills: `All`, `🟢 Easy` (78), `🟡 Medium` (194), and `🔴 Hard` (28).\n* **Learning Status Filter**:\n  * One-click filter pills: `All`, `⚪ Not Started`, `⏳ Attempted`, `✅ Solved`, `🔖 Review`, `⭐ Bookmarked`, and `📝 Notes`.\n  * **Review Status Integration**: Users can flag problems they need to revisit or practice before interviews. Supported in `localStorage` under `progress.review`.\n  * Displayed directly in problem table rows (`🔖` button & pill) and detail modal footer (`🔖 Mark for Review`).\n* **Algorithmic Pattern Filter**:\n  * Dynamic selector populated with algorithmic patterns (e.g. *Hash Map Lookup*, *Two-Pointer Partition*, *Sliding Window Dynamic*, *Binary Search on Answer Space*, *Monotonic Stack Next Greater*).\n* **Bookmarked Status Filter**:\n  * Accessible via the status filter pill or as an independent toggle (`⭐ Bookmarked`).\n\n---\n\n#### B. Sorting Engine\nIntegrated an 8-option sorting engine accessible across both the main Problem Explorer and dedicated Topic pages:\n\n| Sort Key | UI Label | Behavior |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `order_asc` | **Learning Order (1 → 300)** | *Default*: Curated curriculum progression from fundamentals to advanced patterns. |\n| `order_desc` | **Learning Order (300 → 1)** | Reverse curriculum progression. |\n| `title_asc` | **Title (A → Z)** | Lexicographical alphabetical order by problem name. |\n| `title_desc` | **Title (Z → A)** | Reverse alphabetical order. |\n| `diff_asc` | **Difficulty (Easy → Hard)** | Groups: Easy (78) → Medium (194) → Hard (28). |\n| `diff_desc` | **Difficulty (Hard → Easy)** | Groups: Hard (28) → Medium (194) → Easy (78). |\n| `lc_asc` | **LeetCode # (Ascending)** | Ordered by official LeetCode problem number (e.g. 1, 2, 3, 4...). |\n| `lc_desc` | **LeetCode # (Descending)** | Reverse LeetCode number order. |\n\n---\n\n#### C. Pagination & Responsive List Rendering\n* **Configurable Page Size**:\n  * Page size selector in the table metadata bar: `10`, `25` *(default)*, `50`, `100`, or `All (300)`.\n* **Complete Pagination Controls**:\n  * First page (`|←`), Previous (`← Prev`), numbered page buttons with smart ellipsis (`…`), Next (`Next →`), and Last page (`→|`).\n* **Dynamic Range Indicator**:\n  * e.g., *\"Showing 1–25 of 300 problems (Page 1 of 12)\"*.\n* **Smooth Navigation**:\n  * Changing pages smoothly scrolls back to the problem table top.\n\n---\n\n#### D. Unique Problem Route & Dedicated Detail View\n* **URL Hash Router (`initRouter`)**:\n  * Direct route support: `#dsa/problem/:id` and `#problem/:id`.\n  * Navigating directly to (or bookmarking) a URL like `http://localhost:3000/#dsa/problem/1` automatically opens the DSA hub and displays that problem's detail view.\n  * Browser Back / Forward buttons work without breaking page state.\n* **Modal Route Bar & Direct Sharing**:\n  * Every problem detail view displays a direct route badge: `📍 Route: #dsa/problem/1`.\n  * `\"🔗 Copy Problem Link\"` button copies the full shareable URL to the clipboard with confirmation feedback toast (`✓ Link copied to clipboard!`).\n  * Modal footer includes `\"🔖 Mark for Review\"`, `\"⭐ Bookmark\"`, `\"✅ Solved\"`, and `\"▶ Load & Step in Visualizer\"`.\n\n---\n\n#### E. Duplicate Prevention on Problem Import\n* **Import Engine (`importProblems(newProblems, options)`):**\n  * Added programmatic and UI-based importing with duplicate detection across 4 unique criteria:\n    1. **Problem ID (`id`)**: Verifies ID uniqueness.\n    2. **LeetCode Number (`leetcodeNumber`)**: Prevents re-importing identical LeetCode numbers.\n    3. **Normalized Title (`normalizeTitle`)**: Strips whitespace and case to identify duplicate titles.\n    4. **Normalized Source URL (`normalizeUrl`)**: Checks official URL endpoints.\n  * **Duplicate Strategy**:\n    * `skip` *(default)*: Ignores duplicates, preserves existing records and user progress.\n    * `update`: Merges updated fields without altering the existing catalog ID or user completion data.\n  * **Interactive Import Modal (`📥 Import JSON`)**:\n    * Textarea for JSON arrays.\n    * `\"📄 Load Sample\"` button to test import templates.\n    * `\"🔍 Check for Duplicates\"` dry-run button that displays a detailed pre-import report before committing.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Comprehensive Test Verification\n\nAll 5 test suites were executed:\n\n| Test Suite | Focus Area | Tests Run | Result |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| [`test_dsa_phase4.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_dsa_phase4.js) | Search, filters, review status, sorting, pagination, routes, dedup import | **71 / 71** | **PASS (100%)** |\n| [`test_dsa_phase3.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_dsa_phase3.js) | 300 problems schema, LeetCode URLs, notes system, detail modal | **40 / 40** | **PASS (100%)** |\n| [`test_dsa_phase2.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_dsa_phase2.js) | 30-topic library, multi-topic tagging, recommended next problem | **34 / 34** | **PASS (100%)** |\n| [`test_dsa_phase1.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_dsa_phase1.js) | Dashboard metrics, real `localStorage` stats, view switcher | **59 / 59** | **PASS (100%)** |\n| [`test_phase5.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_phase5.js) | Core visualizer engine: Kadane max subarray output = 6 | **82 / 82** | **PASS (100%)** |\n| **Total System Tests** | **Full System & Regression Coverage** | **286 / 286** | **PASS (100%)** |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Files Modified\n\n- [`app_build/dsa_dashboard.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/dsa_dashboard.js): Added review tracking methods, enhanced `getFilteredProblems()` with 8 sort options, updated table rendering with page size selector, added `initRouter()` and route handling, and implemented `importProblems()` and `showImportModal()`.\n- [`app_build/styles.css`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css): Added styling for review buttons, route badge, page size picker, copy-link feedback toast, and import modal components.\n- [`app_build/engine.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/engine.js): **Preserved completely intact.**"}
{"step_index":2179,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:05Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n7. Phase 5: Create a Problem Learning Workspace\n\nWhen a user opens a problem, display a dedicated learning page.\n\nA. Understand the Problem\n\nExplain the problem in simple English.\n\nShow:\n\nWhat the problem asks.\n\nInput and output examples.\n\nExpected output for each example.\n\nImportant constraints.\n\nEdge cases.\n\nWhat the learner needs to calculate or return.\n\nDo not immediately reveal the solution.\n\nB. Learn the Pattern\n\nExplain:\n\nWhich DSA pattern is relevant.\n\nWhy the pattern is useful.\n\nWhich prerequisite concepts are needed.\n\nA small illustrative example.\n\nA simple explanation of the intended approach.\n\nUse built-in, rule-based teaching content. Do not call an AI API.\n\nC. Try It Yourself\n\nProvide a Python editor where the user can write their own solution.\n\nInclude:\n\nRun Code.\n\nRun Tests.\n\nReset Code.\n\nShow Hints.\n\nReveal Reference Solution, with confirmation.\n\nView Test Results.\n\nUse a safe, restricted execution environment. Never execute unrestricted user code on the main application server.\n\nIf the existing execution infrastructure cannot safely support arbitrary Python, implement a restricted interpreter for supported syntax or clearly document the limitation.\n\nD. Visualize Execution\n\nIntegrate with my existing Code Flow Visualizer.\n\nWhen supported Python code is submitted for visualization:\n\nDisplay the actual executing line.\n\nTrack variable values.\n\nExplain conditions and loops.\n\nShow execution history.\n\nSupport Previous Step and Next Step.\n\nPreserve existing animations and beginner explanations.\n\nDo not create a duplicate execution engine unnecessarily.\n\nIf the existing visualizer cannot handle a particular Python construct, explain which construct is unsupported. Never fabricate execution steps or results.\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-27T15:32:05+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
